{"shortDescription":"By Avinash  PBrazilian assets declined on Monday after new polls pointed to an increasingly tight presidential race ahead of next month's election, while assets across the broader region also weakened as surging oil prices curbed risk appetite.In Brazil, the real FX_IDC:USDBRL dropped 0.8%, while t…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["By Avinash  P"]},{"type":"p","children":["Brazilian assets declined on Monday after new polls pointed to an increasingly tight presidential race ahead of next month's election, while assets across the broader region also weakened as surging oil prices curbed risk appetite."]},{"type":"p","children":["In Brazil, the real ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"FX_IDC:USDBRL","text":"FX_IDC:USDBRL"}}," dropped 0.8%, while the local stocks benchmark ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"BMFBOVESPA:IBOV","text":"BMFBOVESPA:IBOV"}}," fell 1.5% after two polls released on Monday showed Brazilian President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva and right-wing Senator Flavio Bolsonaro statistically tied in a potential second-round runoff ahead of next month's election."]},{"type":"p","children":["Lula regained a narrow lead over the eldest son of former President Jair Bolsonaro in a BTG Pactual/Nexus survey, while a separate Quaest poll commissioned by Globo showed the lawmaker numerically ahead for the first time."]},{"type":"p","children":["Brazilian markets had rallied in recent sessions after polls showed Bolsonaro narrowing the gap in the presidential race. Since investors view Bolsonaro as more market-friendly, signs that Lula is regaining ground could pressure local assets."]},{"type":"p","children":["MSCI's Latin American stocks index (.MILA00000PUS) dropped 1.8% to a near-two week low."]},{"type":"p","children":["Separately, Brazil's central bank will cut interest rates by a quarter point for a fifth straight meeting on Wednesday, a Reuters poll of economists found."]},{"type":"p","children":["\"Since the last Copom meeting, the news flow has been mixed for the inflation outlook. The global environment has deteriorated, while domestic indicators continue to point to economic deceleration and disinflation,\" XP analysts said in a note referring to the Brazilian Central bank. \"This combination should reinforce the Copom's cautious stance, though it will not prevent another rate cut.\""]},{"type":"p","children":["At 14.00%, the Selic benchmark rate is one of the highest in the world among major economies. Data on Friday showed the country's annual inflation cooled which paved the way for further rate easing."]},{"type":"p","children":["Overall, the mood was shaky as oil prices climbed after new strikes on Saudi Arabian energy infrastructure and attacks on ships in the Middle East compounded supply concerns."]},{"type":"p","children":["Sustained higher prices continue to stoke inflationary worries, while forcing policymakers to a tighter interest rate environment."]},{"type":"p","children":["Against this backdrop investors will look ahead to the U.S. Federal Reserve's rate decision later in the week, with traders pricing in an 88.7% chance it hikes rate by a quarter point, according to CME's FedWatch tool."]},{"type":"p","children":["U.S. dollar ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"TVC:DXY","text":"TVC:DXY"}}," strengthened to its highest in nearly two weeks, as increasing chances of an imminent rate tightening and higher oil pushed investors to the safe haven asset."]},{"type":"p","children":["An index tracking LatAm currencies (.MILA00000CUS) fell 1.1% to a near two-week low."]},{"type":"p","children":["Chilean peso ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"FX_IDC:USDCLP","text":"FX_IDC:USDCLP"}}," weakened 1.9% to its lowest level in nearly 11 months as copper prices fell to multi-week lows ."]},{"type":"p","children":["The country is the No. 1 exporter of the metal. Local stocks (.MICL00000PUS) eased 2.2%."]},{"type":"p","children":["Mexican peso ",{"typ